From: Librescoot
Subject: [PATCH] fill-extrusion: skip the depth prepass on translucent buildings

When fill-extrusion-opacity is below 1, maplibre-native draws the layer
twice: once into the depth buffer only, with the colour mask off, and
then again for colour with a stencil test. The prepass exists so that on
a building whose own footprint self-overlaps in projection only the
nearest surface is blended.

That prepass runs the full lighting vertex shader on every vertex and
keeps nothing but depth. Measured on the DBC (i.MX6DL, Vivante GC880:
one shader core, one pixel pipe) the buildings layer is vertex-shader
bound, so submitting the geometry a second time is very close to half
the layer's cost:

  stock                 12.7 fps, 60.6 ms in swap
  without the prepass   18.4 fps, 33.6 ms in swap

That is +45% on the map screen. Confirmed vertex-bound rather than fill
bound by scaling fill-extrusion-height to 5%, which leaves the vertex
count untouched and cuts fill area roughly twentyfold: no change (13.6
fps). The same win is available by setting opacity to 1.0, which takes
the identical single-pass branch, but that loses the translucency.

What is given up: back-face culling plus depth write already leaves one
surface per pixel for convex volumes, so ordinary blocks are unaffected.
Only footprints that self-overlap in projection (L-shapes, courtyards,
wings) can now blend a far and a near wall at the same pixel, which at
45% alpha reads as slightly denser rather than as an artifact. Compared
side by side at matched camera positions in Berlin Mitte, no visible
difference.

Upstream still does this on main (render_fill_extrusion_layer.cpp:282,
`const auto doDepthPass = (!opaque || hasPattern);`), so this is not
fixed by moving off the opengl-2 pin. The cleaner fix would be a
depth-only shader variant for the prepass, which would keep correctness
and cost ~10 instructions instead of ~42, but that is a much larger
change for a slightly smaller win.

--- a/vendor/maplibre-native/src/mbgl/renderer/layers/render_fill_extrusion_layer.cpp
+++ b/vendor/maplibre-native/src/mbgl/renderer/layers/render_fill_extrusion_layer.cpp
@@ -153,13 +153,10 @@ void RenderFillExtrusionLayer::render(PaintParameters& parameters) {
             // Draw opaque extrusions
             drawTiles(gfx::StencilMode::disabled(), parameters.colorModeForRenderPass(), "color");
         } else {
-            // Draw transparent buildings in two passes so that only the closest surface is drawn.
-            // First draw all the extrusions into only the depth buffer. No colors are drawn.
-            drawTiles(gfx::StencilMode::disabled(), gfx::ColorMode::disabled(), "depth");
-
-            // Then draw all the extrusions a second time, only coloring fragments if they have the
-            // same depth value as the closest fragment in the previous pass. Use the stencil buffer
-            // to prevent the second draw in cases where we have coincident polygons.
+            // Single pass. The depth prepass upstream runs here submits every
+            // building vertex a second time to fill depth only, which is about
+            // half this layer's cost on the GC880. Back-face culling plus depth
+            // write already resolves convex volumes to one surface per pixel.
             drawTiles(parameters.stencilModeFor3D(), parameters.colorModeForRenderPass(), "color");
         }
     } else {
